scaling t1->t8: oldmain 0.36x -> newmain 3.66x (8bpc), 0.42x -> 3.27x (10bpc).
MT gap to dav1d at t8: 19-21x -> 2.9-3.9x. Frame MD5s identical across all
arms and thread counts per vector. The ab5b81cc "A" section transfers to x64:
the multiplicative barrier x tracker-shard diagnosis was correct, and my
pre-merge "tracker exonerated" conclusion was the exact false-negative that
doc predicts (the attrib arm predated the adaptive block shift).

## 2. NEW DEFECT: x86 LF window race — issue #457

newmain intermittently panics at t>=2 (13/60 sweep cells; 4/12 dedicated t=4
runs): immutable read at src/safe_simd/loopfilter.rs:5081 (compact V-window =
tap_before + 16 rows, memcpy'd) x mutable BlockMut write-back
(picture.rs:1887) of next-sbrow reconstruction. Causal A/B: reverse-applying
054e2ed8 (re-adding the deblock barrier) -> 0/12 panics. Reproduced
independently on WSL 7950X (mt_stress_4k, t=2) and by
tile_threading_overlap::multi_threaded_cdef_lpf_race in 0.13 s. M4: zero
panics, full suite — the window shape is x86-path code the ARM LF rewrite
does not share. Fix shape: exact tap-reach windows in the x86 LF (not the
barrier). CI now runs these gates (c3ea1781); the job is expected red on
x86-64 until #457 lands.

## 3. NEW DEFECT: x86-64 t=1 +50-59% regression — issue #458

Bisected to verify/compose-2, then fine-bisected to **1f09769** ("release a
borrow without taking the shard lock, and re-open the BLOCK_SHIFT ladder"):
oldmain 220.0 -> 1f09769 351.3 ms/f, flat through c003d2f/fd5239f/main.
aarch64 t=1 did NOT regress (verify_compose3 meta §2: comp/base 0.994; the
commit's own M4 A/B said -0.9%), and the sharded tracker per se is exonerated
(attrib tip 762a346c, sharded, measured t=1 220.4 on this rig the previous
day). perf at t=1 on 1f09769: add::<true> 7.4%, add_wide 3.3%, remove_wide
3.3% self — the WIDE path fires at single-thread — and memset+memmove grow
8.3+3.6% -> 13.8+11.8%. Suspect: serial-instance shard/slot configuration
after the occupancy externalization (overflow -> wide promotion), not the
fetch_and itself.

